# The dashboard stores everything in PostgreSQL. The quickest way to a working
# .env is to let the app create the database and write this file for you:
#
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m app.database setup
#
# (it asks once for the PostgreSQL superuser's password). Otherwise copy this
# file to .env and fill it in. With no database configured, nothing is saved
# and sign-in stays closed.
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real credentials.

# --- Storage -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Either set DATABASE_URL outright...
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg2://coteach:change-me@localhost:5432/coteach

# ...or the discrete parts. `setup` finds the port of the newest running
# local PostgreSQL. The Windows installer gives a second version 5433 when an
# older one already holds 5432; docker-compose.yml uses 5434.
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=coteach
DB_USER=coteach
DB_PASSWORD=change-me

# --- Model artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# Header text. Defaults to the academic year containing today, taking
# September as its first month.
# COTEACH_ACADEMIC_YEAR=2026–2027

# --- Backups -------------------------------------------------------------------
# pg_dump is looked up in the PostgreSQL installer's folders. Set this if it
# lives somewhere else.
# COTEACH_PG_BIN=C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\18\bin

# Point the contract at a mounted volume instead of model/artifacts/.
# COTEACH_ARTIFACTS_DIR=/srv/coteach/artifacts

# --- Sessions ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Idle seconds before a session is dropped. Short by default because these are
# shared college lab machines. 3600 = one hour.
# APP_IDLE_TIMEOUT=3600

# --- Accounts ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Accounts live in the database, created with:
#   python -m app.accounts add tutor@st.knust.edu.gh --role tutor
# or a whole cohort from a class list (columns: email, name, role):
#   python -m app.accounts import class.csv --passwords ..\passwords.csv
# A forgotten password is reset with:
#   python -m app.accounts passwd someone@st.knust.edu.gh --generate
# There is deliberately no password in this file: sign-in fails closed until a
# real account exists.
